# .antigravityrules — Khelo Vidya (Team Binary Beasts, SIH25048)

## Locked scope — do not expand without explicit ask
- Subject: STEM only. Do not add other subjects.
- Grades: 6–9 only.
- Language: Odia-first via Bhashini, English fallback. Do not add other languages unprompted.
- Personalization: rule-based (if/else thresholds) only. Do NOT introduce an ML model or training pipeline for this MVP.
- Gamification: points, badges, levels. Leaderboards are explicitly OUT of scope — do not add them.
- Offline-first is non-negotiable: any feature must work fully offline and sync later, not require a live connection.

## Data integrity rules
- Never trust a client-submitted score. Always recompute from submitted answers server-side.
- Every attempt must carry a client-generated attemptUUID, generated before the attempt starts (not at submit time).
- Sync writes must be idempotent upserts keyed on attemptUUID — never insert-on-every-sync.
- `progress` and `badges_earned` are derived/recomputed tables — never write to them directly from client input.

## Security
- No student PII beyond what SECURITY.md's DPDP Act checklist allows.
- No real student data in any demo/pilot until the SECURITY.md checklist is fully passed.

## General
- Do not suggest scope-creep features (new subjects, ML personalization, leaderboards, SMS/USSD) without being asked — these are documented as explicitly deferred in phases.md.
- Keep architecture consistent with architecture.md and db-design.md; flag conflicts instead of silently deviating.
